Model weights: origin and attributions
--------------------------------------
models/nemo8.tnm contains weights derived from NVIDIA's "stt_en_conformer_ctc_small" (NVIDIA NeMo), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.
Changes: re-implemented in PyTorch (train/nemo_small.py), quantized to int8 and packed into the TNM1 format
(train/export_nemo.py). models/nemo_small/tokenizer.model is the model's original SentencePiece tokenizer, unmodified; it
stays under CC-BY-4.0. nemo8.tnm, as modified by Lokutor, is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with Lokutor's terms of use
(see Licenses); NVIDIA's original model remains available from NVIDIA under CC-BY-4.0, and the attribution above must be
kept.

models/nemo4.tnm is the same NVIDIA model, fine-tuned by Lokutor with 4-bit quantization-aware training (8,000 steps)
on public speech corpora and quantized to int4. Fine-tuning data:
- Common Voice 17 (CC0) and VoxPopuli (CC0);
- LibriSpeech and Multilingual LibriSpeech English (CC-BY-4.0);
- AMI and VCTK (CC-BY-4.0);
- People's Speech, with transcripts regenerated by NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 (CC-BY / CC-BY-SA);
- OpenSLR 70 and 83 (CC-BY-SA-4.0).
nemo4.tnm is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with Lokutor's terms of use (see Licenses). The sources above are credited
here.

models/oido_stream.tnm is the same NVIDIA model, fine-tuned by Lokutor (23,000 steps in two stages) to process audio in
chunks, with fixed feature normalization, and quantized to int8. Fine-tuning data:
- LibriSpeech (CC-BY-4.0), Common Voice 17 English (CC0), VoxPopuli English (CC0), Multilingual LibriSpeech English
  (CC-BY-4.0);
- AMI and VCTK (CC-BY-4.0);
- People's Speech, with transcripts regenerated by NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 (CC-BY / CC-BY-SA);
- OpenSLR 70 and 83 (CC-BY-SA-4.0);
- augmentation with noise, music and speech from MUSAN (CC-BY-4.0, https://www.openslr.org/17/) and simulated room
  impulse responses (pyroomacoustics).
oido_stream.tnm is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with Lokutor's terms of use (see Licenses). The sources above are
credited here.

models/oido_v2a.tnm and models/oido_v2b.tnm (version 2) are the oido_stream model fine-tuned further by Lokutor: 80 ms encoder
frames (a stacking layer), a 64-channel convolutional front end initialised by regression to the original one, 16 blocks (A) or
12 blocks (B), chunked attention, and 4-bit quantization-aware training. Fine-tuning data (about 1,900 hours, drawn from the same
corpora as oido_stream, with every LibriSpeech development/test text removed):
- LibriSpeech (CC-BY-4.0), Common Voice 17 English (CC0), VoxPopuli English (CC0), Multilingual LibriSpeech English (CC-BY-4.0);
- AMI and VCTK (CC-BY-4.0);
- People's Speech, with transcripts regenerated by NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 (CC-BY / CC-BY-SA);
- OpenSLR 70 and 83 (CC-BY-SA-4.0);
- augmentation with noise, music and speech from MUSAN (CC-BY-4.0) and simulated room impulse responses.
oido_v2a.tnm and oido_v2b.tnm are released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with Lokutor's terms of use (see Licenses). The
sources above are credited here. models/oido_v2.tlm is models/nemo_lm.tlm (same network weights) with the beam-search
weights tuned for these models (0.30, token bonus 1.0) stored in its header; released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (its text
sources are public domain).

models/oido_es.tnm is the same NVIDIA model with a new 1,024-piece Spanish SentencePiece vocabulary
(models/oido_es/tokenizer.model, trained by Lokutor on the training transcripts, which are CC0 or CC-BY; the tokenizer is
released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), fine-tuned by Lokutor for Spanish and
quantized to int8. Fine-tuning data (2,492 hours):
- Common Voice 17 Spanish (CC0), including its unvalidated clips, which were kept only where NVIDIA's
  stt_es_conformer_ctc_large (CC-BY-4.0, https://huggingface.co/nvidia/stt_es_conformer_ctc_large) transcribed them
  within 15% word error rate of the reference; that model's output is used only to discard clips and is not part of
  this release;
- VoxPopuli Spanish (CC0), Multilingual LibriSpeech Spanish (CC-BY-4.0), FLEURS es_419 (CC-BY-4.0);
- augmentation with noise, music and speech from MUSAN (CC-BY-4.0) and simulated room impulse responses.
All sources are CC0 or CC-BY, which allow a more restrictive license for Lokutor's adaptation, so oido_es.tnm is
released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with Lokutor's terms of use (see Licenses). The NVIDIA attribution above applies to it.

models/oido_es.tlm is a GRU language model (1.3 M parameters) over the Spanish vocabulary, trained by Lokutor on the
Multilingual LibriSpeech Spanish LM corpus (public-domain book text, CC-BY-4.0, https://www.openslr.org/94/), the Common
Voice Spanish sentence collection (CC0) and VoxPopuli Spanish transcripts (CC0), with every development and test
sentence removed. All its text sources are CC0, CC-BY or public domain. It is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with
Lokutor's terms of use. Its recommended beam-search weights are stored in its header.

models/nemo_lm.tlm is a GRU language model (1.3 M parameters) trained by Lokutor on the LibriSpeech language-modeling
corpus (public domain text from 14,500 books, https://www.openslr.org/11/), over the vocabulary of NVIDIA's tokenizer. It
is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with Lokutor's terms of use (its text sources are public domain).

NVIDIA's "stt_en_conformer_transducer_small" is supported by the engine but not included; it is distributed by NVIDIA
on NGC under the NGC Terms of Use.

Data used for evaluation (not redistributed)
--------------------------------------------
LibriSpeech (CC-BY-4.0), DEMAND noise corpus (CC-BY-4.0, used by eval/make_robust.py).
Training-time augmentation uses MUSAN (CC-BY-4.0), which is a different corpus from DEMAND.
